// STORY CONTENT IS STORED HERE. Replace any paragraph later without touching the UI.
const STORY = [{"number":1,"title":"The Fire at Dawn","romanTitle":"Aag ka Aaghaz","meta":"Sand / Earth","en":["Aran woke before the sun because his mother had stopped breathing beside the fire. For one terrible moment he thought she was dead. Then Benna coughed, opened her eyes, and pushed his hand away. “Get wood,” she whispered. “Fear burns faster than fire.” It was the sort of thing she said whenever the world became impossible, which meant she had said it often.","Their camp stood beneath a limestone ridge above the southern river. Raan, Aran’s father, had chosen the place because three sides were protected by stone and the fourth could be watched from the trees. Their family had lived there through the last dry season with Kian, Aran’s younger brother, learning to set snares and Benna turning roots, grain and dried meat into meals that never tasted as small as the portions.","That morning the river was low. Fish flashed between stones. Aran carried a woven basket and checked the traps while Kian searched for edible bulbs. They were laughing about a rabbit that had stolen grain from their store when the first bird suddenly rose from the reeds.","Raan saw it too. He did not shout. He simply lifted his spear. “Home,” he said. The family moved instantly. Years of living together had taught them that panic wasted breath. Benna gathered the children. Aran grabbed the water skins. Kian carried the small stone axe even though he was too young to use it properly.","Smoke appeared beyond the ridge. Then another column. Their village was burning.","Raan stared at the smoke for one heartbeat. Then he made the decision that would divide their lives into before and after. They would not run toward the village. They would run north, through the reed valley, where the enemy would expect hunters to avoid the marsh.","They moved through waist-high grass while distant shouting rolled across the land. Aran wanted to turn back for neighbors, tools and stored food. Benna caught his arm. “A family that dies trying to save everyone saves no one,” she said. The words hurt because they were true.","At the marsh edge they found footprints. Many people had passed recently. Raan knelt and studied them. “Ash Hunters,” he said. Their faces were painted with gray clay, and they had attacked several settlements along the river. But Raan looked more worried than frightened.","“They are not here for grain,” he said.","That night the family hid beneath a fallen fig tree. They divided the last dried meat into equal pieces. Kian complained that Aran had received the largest piece. Aran gave him half. Benna smiled without saying anything. Raan watched his sons and quietly moved his own piece into Kian’s hand.","Before dawn, a horn sounded from the ridge. The enemy had found them.","Raan pushed a small black stone into Aran’s palm. It carried an old symbol, three lines inside a circle. “If I am separated from you, keep this hidden,” he said. “Do not trade it. Do not show it. And never follow anyone who says they know what it means.”","Aran wanted to ask why. An arrow struck the tree above them.","They ran.","The marsh became a maze of mud, reeds and black water. Aran carried Kian when the boy’s foot sank into a hidden hole. Benna moved behind them, breaking branches to confuse their trail. Raan stayed last.","Then came the sound Aran would remember for the rest of his life: his father shouting for them to keep going.","Aran turned. Raan was surrounded.","Their eyes met across the reeds. Raan raised his spear, not in surrender but in command. Go.","Aran dragged Kian forward. Benna followed, crying silently. Behind them came steel striking wood, men shouting, and then silence.","By sunset they reached the river. The current was violent from distant rain. Benna wanted to cross. Aran wanted to wait. Kian was exhausted.","They built a crude raft from driftwood and vine. Aran tied the bundles while Benna held Kian. It was ugly, unstable and probably stupid. It was also their only chance.","Halfway across, the rope snapped.","The raft spun. Kian fell into the water.","Aran jumped after him.","The river swallowed both brothers. Aran found Kian by touch, wrapped an arm around him and kicked toward the surface. When they finally reached the opposite bank, Benna was waiting on her knees.","She pulled both sons against her.","For a few moments they were simply a family again.","Then Aran looked back across the river.","Raan was gone.","The first night of their new life began without him. They had little food, one stone axe, two knives, three water skins and a fire-making stone. Behind them was an enemy. Ahead was wilderness.","Benna divided the remaining grain into three portions and buried two beneath a marked tree.","“Why hide food?” Kian asked.","“Because tomorrow we may need to remember where today ended,” she said.","Aran watched the fire. The black stone in his hand felt warm.","Somewhere beyond the dark ridge, a horn answered another horn.","The chase had begun."],"ur":["Aran suraj nikalne se pehle jaag gaya, kyun ke us ki walida Benna aag ke paas khamosh leti thi. Ek lamhe ke liye Aran ko laga ke woh mar chuki hai. Phir Benna ne khansi ki, aankhen kholin aur us ka haath hata diya. “Lakri lao,” us ne dheemi awaaz mein kaha. “Dar aag se zyada jaldi phailta hai.”","Un ka dera darya ke upar limestone ki chattan ke neeche tha. Raan, Aran ka walid, hamesha aisi jagah chunta tha jahan teen taraf pathar aur chauthi taraf jungle ki nazar ho. Khandan ne sukhe mausam ko yahin guzara tha. Kian, Aran ka chhota bhai, phanday lagana seekh raha tha aur Benna jadon, anaaj aur sukhe gosht se aisa khana banati thi jo chhota hote hue bhi ghar jaisa lagta tha.","Us subah darya ka pani kam tha. Machhliyan patharon ke darmiyan chamak rahi thin. Aran tokri le kar phanday dekh raha tha aur Kian khane wali jaden dhoond raha tha jab achanak parindon ka poora jhund reeds se upar uth gaya.","Raan ne bhi dekh liya. Us ne cheekha nahi. Sirf apna neza uthaya. “Ghar,” us ne kaha. Khandan foran chal pada. Saalon ki saath rehne ki aadat ne unhein sikha diya tha ke ghabrahat saans zaya karti hai. Benna ne bachon ko sambhala, Aran ne pani ki mashken uthain aur Kian ne chhoti pathar ki kulhari pakri.","Chattan ke paar se dhuan uth raha tha. Phir doosra dhuan. Un ki basti jal rahi thi.","Raan ne ek pal ke liye dhuan dekha, phir faisla kiya. Woh basti ki taraf wapas nahi jayenge. Woh reeds wali wadi se uttar ki taraf jayenge, jahan dushman shikariyon ko jana pasand nahi karte the.","Dal-dal tak pohanch kar unhein bohat se qadam nazar aaye. Raan ghutnon ke bal baitha aur nishan dekhe. “Ash Hunters,” us ne kaha. Ye log kai bastiyon par hamla kar chuke the. Lekin Raan ka chehra sirf khaufzada nahi tha. Woh pareshan tha.","“Ye log anaaj ke liye nahi aaye,” us ne kaha.","Us raat woh ek gire hue anjeer ke darakht ke neeche chupay. Sukhe gosht ko teen hisson mein baanta gaya. Kian ne shikayat ki ke Aran ko sab se bara hissa mila hai. Aran ne apna aadha hissa usay de diya. Benna muskurai. Raan ne chupke se apna hissa bhi Kian ke haath mein rakh diya.","Subah se pehle chattan se ek seeng ki awaaz aayi. Dushman un tak pohanch gaya tha.","Raan ne Aran ki hatheli mein chhota siyah pathar rakha. Us par teen lakeeron ke andar ek daira bana tha. “Agar hum alag ho jayen to ise chhupa kar rakhna,” us ne kaha. “Na isay bechna, na kisi ko dikhana. Aur jo bhi kahe ke woh iska matlab janta hai, us ke peeche mat jana.”","Aran sawal karna chahta tha. Tabhi ek teer darakht ke upar laga.","Sab bhaag pade.","Dal-dal mitti, reeds aur siyah pani ka jaal ban gayi. Aran ne Kian ko uthaya jab us ka paon chhupe hue gaddhe mein phans gaya. Benna un ke peeche chalti rahi aur jaan boojh kar shakhain todti gayi taake nishan uljhen. Raan sab se peeche tha.","Phir Aran ne woh awaaz suni jo woh zindagi bhar nahi bhool sakta tha: us ka walid cheekh raha tha ke rukna mat.","Aran ne peeche dekha. Raan chaar aadmiyon ke darmiyan tha.","Un ki nazrein mili. Raan ne apna neza uthaya. Us ka ishara sirf ek tha. Bhaago.","Aran ne Kian ko kheench kar aage kiya. Benna roti hui un ke peeche thi. Peeche se hathyar takrane aur aadmiyon ki cheekhein sunai deti rahin. Phir khamoshi.","Shaam tak woh darya tak pohanch gaye. Pani door ki barish ki wajah se tez tha. Benna paar jana chahti thi. Aran rukna chahta tha. Kian thak chuka tha.","Unhon ne driftwood, belon aur rassi se ek chhota raft banaya. Woh badsurat aur khatarnak tha, lekin un ke paas doosra raasta nahi tha.","Darya ke beech rassi toot gayi.","Kian pani mein gir gaya.","Aran us ke peeche kood gaya.","Thande pani ne dono ko nigal liya. Aran ne Kian ko pakra aur use apne saath satah ki taraf kheench laya. Jab dono doosre kinare pohanchay to Benna ghutnon ke bal un ka intezar kar rahi thi.","Us ne dono beton ko galay laga liya.","Kuch lamhon ke liye woh sirf ek khandan thay.","Phir Aran ne darya ke doosre kinare dekha.","Raan gayab tha.","Un ki nayi zindagi ki pehli raat us ke baghair shuru hui. Un ke paas thora sa khana, ek pathar ki kulhari, do chhuriyan, teen pani ki mashken aur aag jalane ka pathar tha. Peeche dushman tha. Aage jungle.","Benna ne bacha hua anaaj teen hisson mein baanta aur do hisse ek nishan wale darakht ke neeche daba diye.","Kian ne poocha, “Khana kyun chhupa rahi ho?”","Benna ne kaha, “Kal humein yaad rakhna hoga ke aaj kahan khatam hua tha.”","Aran ne aag ko dekha. Us ke haath mein siyah pathar garam ho gaya.","Andheri wadi ke paar se ek seeng ki awaaz ka jawab doosri seeng ne diya.","Shikar shuru ho chuka tha."]},{"number":2,"title":"The River of Teeth","romanTitle":"Danton Wala Darya","meta":"River / Moss","en":["They followed the river north for three days. Benna made the family move before sunrise, rest during the hottest hours and travel again when shadows lengthened. Aran learned quickly that survival was mostly repetition: check water, check food, check feet, check the sky, then check the people beside you.","Their first meal was a handful of roasted seeds and a fish Aran caught with a sharpened bone. He had no net, so he learned to wait in shallow water and strike only when the fish turned sideways. Kian called him a great hunter. Aran knew better. Luck had simply been generous.","The second day was not generous.","A wild boar charged from the reeds. Aran threw a spear that missed. Benna pulled Kian behind a tree. The boar struck Aran hard enough to throw him into mud. He survived because Kian, terrified and furious, threw the stone axe.","The axe hit the boar's shoulder.","The animal fled.","For several seconds nobody spoke.","Then Benna laughed. It was the first real laugh since Raan disappeared.","They followed the blood trail and found the animal dead near the river. The family spent the afternoon cleaning it, preserving the best meat with smoke and salt, and turning the hide into a covering. Aran learned how much work was hidden inside the word food.","That evening they ate until they were full.","Kian fell asleep beside Benna.","Aran sat with his back against a tree and sharpened a new spear. He used a straight branch, heated the end, hardened it in the coals and fixed a chipped stone point with resin and sinew.","Benna watched him.","“Your father would be proud.”","Aran looked down.","“He would tell me the point is crooked.”","“He would.”","They both smiled.","The next morning they found a settlement abandoned beside the river. Doors were open. Clay pots were broken. A grain store had been emptied. There were no bodies.","Aran found footprints leading north.","Ash Hunters.","Benna wanted to leave immediately, but Aran discovered something in the dust: a child's bracelet made from red seeds.","Kian picked it up.","“Someone was here.”","“Someone is still here,” Benna said.","A stone flew from the trees and struck the ground.","They ran.","The attack was brief. Three enemies appeared, but Aran had already prepared a trap. He had stretched vine between two roots and covered it with leaves. One hunter fell hard enough to drop his club. Benna took the club and threw it into the river.","The family escaped into a narrow canyon.","That night they heard the enemy searching above them.","Aran wanted to attack. Benna refused.","“A trap you don't need is a trap you should not build.”","They waited.","Hours later, the voices disappeared.","At dawn they found a cave high above the river. Inside were old charcoal marks and animal bones. Someone had lived there long ago.","Aran discovered a small clay tablet under a flat stone. It carried the same three-line symbol as his father's black stone.","Benna touched it and went pale.","“You know it,” Aran said.","She shook her head.","“I know that your father wanted it forgotten.”","Before Aran could press her, Kian shouted from outside.","A figure stood across the river.","A woman.","She raised one hand.","She did not carry a weapon.","Her name was Sera."],"ur":["Woh followed the darya north for three days. Benna made khandan move se pehle surajrise, rest during the hottest hours aur travel again when shadows lengthened. Aran learned quickly that zinda rehna tha mostly repetition: check pani, check khana, check feet, check the aasman, then check the people beside you.","Un ka first khana tha a handful of roasted seeds aur a fish Aran caught ke saath a sharpened bone. Woh ke paas no net, so he learned to wait in shallow pani aur strike only when the fish turned sideways. Kian called him a great shikari. Aran knew better. Luck ke paas simply been generous.","The second day tha not generous.","A wild boar charged se the reeds. Aran threw a neza that missed. Benna pulled Kian ke peeche a tree. The boar struck Aran hard enough to throw him mein mud. Woh zinda rehnad because Kian, terrified aur furious, threw the pathar kulhari.","The kulhari hit the boar's shoulder.","The animal fled.","For several seconds nobody spoke.","Then Benna laughed. It tha the first real laugh since Raan disappeared.","Woh followed the khoon trail aur found the animal dead near the darya. Khandan spent the afternoon cleaning it, preserving the best gosht ke saath dhuan aur salt, aur turning the hide mein a covering. Aran learned how much work tha hidden inside the word khana.","That evening they ate until they thay full.","Kian fell asleep beside Benna.","Aran sat ke saath us ka back against a tree aur sharpened a new neza. Woh used a straight branch, heated the end, hardened it in the coals aur fixed a chipped pathar point ke saath resin aur sinew.","Benna watched him.","“Your walid would be proud.”","Aran looked down.","“Woh would tell me the point hai crooked.”","“Woh would.”","Woh both smiled.","The next subah they found a settlement abandoned beside the darya. Doors thay open. Clay pots thay broken. A anaaj store ke paas been emptied. There thay no bodies.","Aran found footprints leading north.","Ash Hunters.","Benna wanted to leave immediately, lekin Aran discovered something in the dust: a child's bracelet made se red seeds.","Kian picked it up.","“Someone tha here.”","“Someone hai still here,” Benna said.","A pathar flew se the trees aur struck the ground.","Woh ran.","The attack tha brief. Three enemies appeared, lekin Aran ke paas already prepared a phanda. Woh ke paas stretched vine between two roots aur covered it ke saath leaves. One shikari fell hard enough to drop us ka club. Benna took the club aur threw it mein the darya.","Khandan escaped mein a narrow canyon.","That raat they heard the dushman searching above them.","Aran wanted to attack. Benna refused.","“A phanda you don't need hai a phanda you should not build.”","Woh waited.","Hours later, the voices disappeared.","At dawn they found a cave high above the darya. Inside thay old charcoal marks aur animal bones. Someone ke paas lived there long ago.","Aran discovered a small clay tablet under a flat pathar. It carried the same three-line symbol as us ka walid's black pathar.","Benna touched it aur went pale.","“You know it,” Aran said.","Woh shook us ka head.","“I know that your walid wanted it forgotten.”","Before Aran could press her, Kian shouted se outside.","A figure stood across the darya.","A woman.","Woh raised one hand.","Woh did not carry a hathyar.","Us ka name tha Sera."]},{"number":3,"title":"The Silent Camp","romanTitle":"Khamosh Dera","meta":"Ash / Stone","en":["Sera did not ask permission before entering their camp. She simply sat near the fire, examined the food, and told Kian that his knot was useless. Kian immediately disliked her.","Aran liked her for exactly the same reason.","Sera came from a hill clan farther north. Her people hunted red deer, grew a small amount of barley and traded stone blades along the river. She knew the Ash Hunters and had lost a brother to them.","She also knew Raan.","That fact changed everything.","Sera told Aran that his father had once traveled to the northern valley with her own father. They had found ruins there, older than any living settlement. The ruins contained maps, tools and a sealed stone chamber.","“What was inside?” Aran asked.","“Your father never opened it.”","“Why?”","“Because he was afraid of what the people before us had built.”","Aran wanted to dismiss the story. Instead he remembered the warm black stone.","Sera looked at it.","“The Ash Hunters want that.”","Benna finally spoke.","“No. They want the boy.”","Aran looked at his mother.","The silence that followed was worse than an answer.","That evening Sera taught Aran to make a fish trap from reeds and stones. They built a narrow channel that forced fish into a basket. Kian insisted on checking it first and returned with three fish and a huge grin.","The family cooked them with wild onion and crushed seeds.","For a brief hour, the world felt normal.","Then Sera saw smoke.","Not cooking smoke.","A signal.","She ordered them to extinguish the fire.","They scattered cold ash over the coals and hid among rocks.","Five Ash Hunters entered the valley.","Their leader was a scarred man named Varek.","Aran recognized him immediately.","Varek stood beside the dead fire and smiled.","“Raan's son,” he called. “Your father has run long enough.”","Aran stayed silent.","Varek placed a wooden marker in the ground.","A red mark painted across it.","“When the moon reaches the mountain, we come for you.”","The hunters left.","Sera waited until their footsteps vanished.","“They are giving us time.”","“Why?” Aran asked.","“Because they want you frightened.”","Benna looked at the red mark.","“Then we should make them frightened too.”","It was the first time Aran had heard his mother speak like a warrior.","That night the family built their first deliberate defensive camp. They dug shallow pits, placed sharpened stakes beneath leaves and created a second escape path toward the river.","They also divided their food into hidden stores.","Aran realized something important.","A weapon was not only a spear.","A weapon could be a path, a hidden meal, a false trail, a good knot, a quiet fire.","Strategy was simply surviving before the fight began.","Near midnight, an arrow landed beside Aran.","No one had heard the hunter.","Sera looked toward the ridge.","“They are testing us.”","Aran picked up the arrow.","Its shaft carried the same red paint as Varek's marker.","The family would not sleep safely again."],"ur":["Sera did not ask permission se pehle entering un ka dera. Woh simply sat near the aag, examined the khana, aur told Kian that us ka knot tha useless. Kian immediately disliked her.","Aran liked us ka for exactly the same reason.","Sera came se a hill qabeela fartus ka north. Us ka people hunted red deer, grew a small amount of barley aur traded pathar blades along the darya. Woh knew the Ash Hunters aur ke paas lost a bhai to them.","Woh also knew Raan.","That fact changed everything.","Sera told Aran that us ka walid ke paas once traveled to the northern wadi ke saath us ka own walid. Woh ke paas found ruins there, older than any living settlement. The ruins contained maps, auzars aur a sealed pathar chamber.","“What tha inside?” Aran asked.","“Your walid never opened it.”","“Why?”","“Because he tha afraid of what the people se pehle us ke paas built.”","Aran wanted to dismiss the story. Instead he remembered the warm black pathar.","Sera looked at it.","“The Ash Hunters want that.”","Benna finally spoke.","“No. Woh want the boy.”","Aran looked at us ka walida.","The silence that followed tha worse than an answer.","That evening Sera taught Aran to make a fish phanda se reeds aur pathars. Woh built a narrow channel that forced fish mein a basket. Kian insisted on checking it first aur returned ke saath three fish aur a huge grin.","Khandan cooked them ke saath wild onion aur crushed seeds.","For a brief hour, the duniya felt normal.","Then Sera saw dhuan.","Not cooking dhuan.","A signal.","Woh ordered them to extinguish the aag.","Woh scattered cold ash over the coals aur hid among rocks.","Five Ash Hunters entered the wadi.","Un ka leader tha a scarred man named Varek.","Aran recognized him immediately.","Varek stood beside the dead aag aur smiled.","“Raan's son,” he called. “Your walid has run long enough.”","Aran stayed silent.","Varek placed a wooden marker in the ground.","A red mark painted across it.","“When the moon reaches the pahaar, we come for you.”","The shikaris left.","Sera waited until un ka footsteps vanished.","“Woh hain giving us time.”","“Why?” Aran asked.","“Because they want you frightened.”","Benna looked at the red mark.","“Then we should make them frightened too.”","It tha the first time Aran ke paas heard us ka walida speak like a warrior.","That raat khandan built un ka first deliberate defensive dera. Woh dug shallow pits, placed sharpened stakes beneath leaves aur created a second escape path toward the darya.","Woh also divided un ka khana mein hidden stores.","Aran realized something important.","A hathyar tha not only a neza.","A hathyar could be a path, a hidden khana, a false trail, a good knot, a quiet aag.","Strategy tha simply surviving se pehle the fight began.","Near midraat, an arrow zameened beside Aran.","No one ke paas heard the shikari.","Sera looked toward the ridge.","“Woh hain testing us.”","Aran picked up the arrow.","Its shaft carried the same red paint as Varek's marker.","Khandan would not sleep safely again."]},{"number":4,"title":"The Hunter's Law","romanTitle":"Shikari ka Qanoon","meta":"Forest / Bronze","en":["By morning the camp was empty.","They left behind cold ashes, false footprints and a broken basket. Their real trail followed a stream hidden beneath reeds.","Sera led them toward the forest.","The forest changed the rules.","There was less open ground, fewer fish and more predators. Aran learned to recognize paw prints, damaged bark and bird calls. Kian learned which berries were safe by watching Benna. Benna learned that Sera could climb trees faster than either of her sons.","They hunted deer for two days without success.","On the third morning Aran found a fresh trail.","He did not chase it.","He built a plan.","He and Sera placed a stone funnel between two trees. Benna waited downwind with a spear. Kian stayed hidden and watched the rear.","The deer appeared at noon.","It sensed them.","Instead of running toward the trap, it turned.","Kian remembered the plan and threw a stone behind it.","The deer changed direction.","Benna struck first.","The animal fell.","No one celebrated.","They thanked it quietly and used nearly everything: meat for food, hide for clothing, sinew for cord, bone for hooks and antler for a new tool.","That evening they ate roasted meat and barley cakes Sera had carried from her clan.","Kian asked if they were becoming hunters.","Benna replied, “We are becoming difficult to kill.”","The next day they found a bronze-colored piece of metal in an old campfire.","It was not bronze. It was copper.","Sera examined it.","“Someone here knows metal.”","Aran looked toward the northern hills.","Their journey was taking them closer to something old.","At sunset they discovered a narrow cave with painted walls.","The drawings showed a family crossing a river.","A mother.","Two children.","A man holding a black stone.","Aran touched the wall.","The image was thousands of years old, yet the family looked almost exactly like his own.","Benna began to cry.","She had seen the drawings before.","She admitted that Raan had once told her the story of the First Family, people who had survived a great drought and built the first stone refuge in Auran.","“Why did you never tell me?” Aran asked.","“Because your father wanted you to have a childhood.”","“I don't have one anymore.”","Benna looked at him.","“Then do not let them take your future too.”","That night Aran made a decision.","They would not merely run.","They would find Raan.","If he was dead, they would learn why.","If he was alive, they would bring him home.","And if the Ash Hunters were protecting a secret, Aran would uncover it.","At dawn, they found Varek's tracks.","He was following them alone.","That meant he was confident.","Or desperate."],"ur":["By subah the dera tha empty.","Woh left ke peeche cold ashes, false footprints aur a broken basket. Un ka real trail followed a stream hidden beneath reeds.","Sera led them toward the jangal.","The jangal changed the rules.","There tha less open ground, fewer fish aur more predators. Aran learned to recognize paw prints, damaged bark aur bird calls. Kian learned which berries thay safe by watching Benna. Benna learned that Sera could climb trees faster than eitus ka of us ka sons.","Woh hunted deer for two days ke baghair success.","On the third subah Aran found a fresh trail.","Woh did not chase it.","Woh built a mansuba.","Woh aur Sera placed a pathar funnel between two trees. Benna waited downwind ke saath a neza. Kian stayed hidden aur watched the rear.","The deer appeared at noon.","It sensed them.","Instead of running toward the phanda, it turned.","Kian remembered the mansuba aur threw a pathar ke peeche it.","The deer changed direction.","Benna struck first.","The animal fell.","No one celebrated.","Woh thanked it quietly aur used nearly everything: gosht for khana, hide for clothing, sinew for cord, bone for hooks aur antler for a new auzar.","That evening they ate roasted gosht aur barley cakes Sera ke paas carried se us ka qabeela.","Kian asked if they thay becoming shikaris.","Benna replied, “We hain becoming difficult to kill.”","The next day they found a bronze-colored piece of metal in an old deraaag.","It tha not bronze. It tha copper.","Sera examined it.","“Someone here knows metal.”","Aran looked toward the northern hills.","Un ka journey tha taking them closer to something old.","At surajset they discovered a narrow cave ke saath painted walls.","The drawings showed a family crossing a darya.","A walida.","Two bachay.","A man holding a black pathar.","Aran touched the wall.","The image tha thousands of years old, yet khandan looked almost exactly like us ka own.","Benna began to cry.","Woh ke paas seen the drawings before.","Woh admitted that Raan ke paas once told us ka the story of the First Family, people who ke paas zinda rehnad a great drought aur built the first pathar refuge in Auran.","“Why did you never tell me?” Aran asked.","“Because your walid wanted you to have a childhood.”","“I don't have one anymore.”","Benna looked at him.","“Then do not let them take your future too.”","That raat Aran made a decision.","Woh would not merely run.","Woh would find Raan.","If he tha dead, they would learn why.","If he tha alive, they would bring him ghar.","And if the Ash Hunters thay protecting a secret, Aran would uncover it.","At dawn, they found Varek's tracks.","Woh tha following them alone.","That meant he tha confident.","Or desperate."]},{"number":5,"title":"The Valley of Bones","romanTitle":"Haddiyon ki Wadi","meta":"Bone / Dust","en":["The valley of bones began after the third ridge.","There were animal skulls everywhere, bleached white by the sun. Deer, wild cattle, wolves and something much larger that Aran could not identify.","Sera warned them not to camp there.","They did anyway.","They needed water.","At the center of the valley stood a dry stone well.","Aran climbed down using old footholds.","Halfway down he found damp soil.","He dug with his hands.","Water appeared.","The family worked for hours to clear the well.","By sunset they had enough to fill every container.","Then Kian found a skeleton beneath the mud.","It was human.","Around its wrist was a copper bracelet marked with three lines inside a circle.","Aran removed it carefully.","Sera stared.","“This is older than the Ash Hunters.”","“How old?”","“Older than our grandfathers' grandfathers.”","The valley contained dozens of human bones.","They were not all killed by violence.","Some showed signs of starvation.","Others had injuries from stone tools.","Aran understood that the place had once been a refuge.","And something had destroyed it.","That night they heard drums.","Varek's people had found them.","There were too many to fight.","Sera proposed a trick.","They would make the enemy believe the family had fled east.","They lit a small fire, placed stones around it and dragged a branch through the dust to create false tracks.","Then they hid in the valley itself.","The plan worked.","The hunters followed the false trail.","Aran and Sera moved through the bones toward the opposite ridge.","They discovered a stone door.","No handle.","Only the symbol.","Aran pressed the black stone against it.","The door opened.","Inside was a chamber filled with old tools.","Stone blades.","Bone needles.","Copper hooks.","Clay jars.","A wooden frame covered with dried animal skin.","It was not treasure.","It was knowledge.","Methods for storing grain.","Methods for collecting rain.","Methods for building traps.","Methods for preserving meat.","Aran understood why Varek wanted it.","A tribe with these tools could survive droughts that killed others.","It could control food.","It could control people.","At the far end of the chamber was a wall map.","Three valleys connected by rivers.","A mountain marked with the same symbol.","And beneath it, a red line.","Sera whispered, “The Stone Gate.”","Aran looked at her.","“What is it?”","“The place your father was trying to reach.”","A sound came from outside.","Varek had entered the valley.","Aran shut the door.","They had found the secret.","But now the enemy had found them."],"ur":["The wadi of bones began ke baad the third ridge.","There thay animal skulls everywhere, bleached white by the suraj. Deer, wild cattle, wolves aur something much larger that Aran could not identify.","Sera warned them not to dera there.","Woh did anyway.","Woh needed pani.","At the center of the wadi stood a dry pathar well.","Aran climbed down using old footholds.","Halfway down he found damp soil.","Woh dug ke saath us ka hands.","Pani appeared.","Khandan worked for hours to clear the well.","By surajset they ke paas enough to fill every container.","Then Kian found a skeleton beneath the mud.","It tha human.","Around its wrist tha a copper bracelet marked ke saath three lines inside a circle.","Aran removed it carefully.","Sera stared.","“Tus ka hai older than the Ash Hunters.”","“How old?”","“Older than our grandwalids' grandwalids.”","The wadi contained dozens of human bones.","Woh thay not all killed by violence.","Some showed signs of starvation.","Others ke paas injuries se pathar auzars.","Aran understood that the place ke paas once been a refuge.","And something ke paas destroyed it.","That raat they heard drums.","Varek's people ke paas found them.","There thay too many to fight.","Sera proposed a trick.","Woh would make the dushman believe khandan ke paas fled east.","Woh lit a small aag, placed pathars around it aur dragged a branch through the dust to create false tracks.","Then they hid in the wadi itself.","The mansuba worked.","The shikaris followed the false trail.","Aran aur Sera moved through the bones toward the opposite ridge.","Woh discovered a pathar darwaza.","No handle.","Only the symbol.","Aran pressed the black pathar against it.","The darwaza opened.","Inside tha a chamber filled ke saath old auzars.","Stone blades.","Bone needles.","Copper hooks.","Clay jars.","A wooden frame covered ke saath dried animal skin.","It tha not treasure.","It tha knowledge.","Methods for storing anaaj.","Methods for collecting barish.","Methods for building phandas.","Methods for preserving gosht.","Aran understood why Varek wanted it.","A tribe ke saath these auzars could zinda rehna droughts that killed others.","It could control khana.","It could control people.","At the far end of the chamber tha a wall map.","Three wadis connected by daryas.","A pahaar marked ke saath the same symbol.","And beneath it, a red line.","Sera whispered, “The Stone Gate.”","Aran looked at her.","“What hai it?”","“The place your walid tha trying to reach.”","A sound came se outside.","Varek ke paas entered the wadi.","Aran shut the darwaza.","Woh ke paas found the secret.","But now the dushman ke paas found them."]},{"number":6,"title":"The Winter Store","romanTitle":"Sardi ka Zakhira","meta":"Smoke / Grain","en":["Winter came early.","The family reached a sheltered valley where reeds grew beside a narrow lake. Sera's clan had abandoned an old storage hut there, and Benna decided it could become a home.","They repaired the roof with grass, bark and hide.","They dug a drainage channel around the walls.","They built a raised platform for sleeping.","They stored smoked meat in clay jars.","Kian became responsible for collecting dry wood.","Aran built snares.","Sera taught them how to read the wind.","For the first time since Raan disappeared, they were not running.","They were preparing.","Aran counted their supplies every morning.","Meat: twenty-seven days.","Grain: eighteen.","Water: enough for four days if the lake froze.","Salt: almost none.","Firewood: eight days.","He wrote the numbers into a clay tablet.","Benna laughed when she saw it.","“You count everything now.”","“Because everything matters.”","She touched his shoulder.","“Your father would be proud.”","Aran looked toward the empty doorway.","“I wish he were here.”","That night Kian asked whether their father was dead.","Benna did not answer.","Aran did.","“We don't know.”","Kian stared into the fire.","“Then he isn't dead.”","The certainty in the boy's voice made Aran smile.","Weeks passed.","They learned to live with the cold.","They made heavier clothing from hide.","They created bone needles.","They trapped rabbits.","They gathered roots.","They fermented a small batch of grain into a sour drink that Kian hated and Benna secretly enjoyed.","The family laughed again.","Then a stranger arrived.","An old man carrying a white wolf skin.","He called himself Oren.","He claimed to be a trader.","Sera did not trust him.","Aran offered him water anyway.","Oren stared at the black stone hanging around Aran's neck.","His face changed.","“Where did you get that?”","Aran reached for his spear.","Oren raised both hands.","“I knew your father.”","The old man told them Raan was alive.","He had been captured by Varek.","Aran nearly attacked him from relief and anger.","Oren continued.","Raan had been taken to the Red Camp, a fortified settlement beyond the western ridge.","He was being forced to explain the Stone Gate.","“Why hasn't Varek killed him?” Aran asked.","“Because your father is the only living person who knows how to open it.”","Aran looked at his family.","The winter had protected them.","Now winter had become a cage.","They needed a plan.","Oren said the Red Camp was guarded by twelve men.","Aran counted their weapons.","Two spears.","One bow.","A stone axe.","Three knives.","Sera had the best bow.","Benna knew the land.","Kian knew the hidden paths.","They were not an army.","They did not need to be.","They needed to become invisible.","Aran began drawing a map in the dirt.","The rescue would begin after the next storm."],"ur":["Winter came early.","Khandan reached a panahed wadi where reeds grew beside a narrow lake. Sera's qabeela ke paas abandoned an old storage hut there, aur Benna decided it could become a ghar.","Woh repaired the roof ke saath grass, bark aur hide.","Woh dug a dbarishage channel around the walls.","Woh built a raised platform for sleeping.","Woh stored dhuand gosht in clay jars.","Kian became responsible for collecting dry wood.","Aran built snares.","Sera taught them how to read the wind.","For the first time since Raan disappeared, they thay not running.","Woh thay preparing.","Aran counted un ka supplies every subah.","Meat: twenty-seven days.","Gbarish: eighteen.","Pani: enough for four days if the lake froze.","Salt: almost none.","Aagwood: eight days.","Woh wrote the numbers mein a clay tablet.","Benna laughed when she saw it.","“You count everything now.”","“Because everything matters.”","Woh touched us ka shoulder.","“Your walid would be proud.”","Aran looked toward the empty darwazaway.","“I wish he thay here.”","That raat Kian asked whetus ka un ka walid tha dead.","Benna did not answer.","Aran did.","“We don't know.”","Kian stared mein the aag.","“Then he isn't dead.”","The certainty in the boy's voice made Aran smile.","Weeks passed.","Woh learned to live ke saath the cold.","Woh made heavier clothing se hide.","Woh created bone needles.","Woh phandaped rabbits.","Woh gathered roots.","Woh fermented a small batch of anaaj mein a sour drink that Kian hated aur Benna secretly enjoyed.","Khandan laughed again.","Then a stranger arrived.","An old man carrying a white bheriya skin.","Woh called himself Oren.","Woh claimed to be a trader.","Sera did not trust him.","Aran offered him pani anyway.","Oren stared at the black pathar hanging around Aran's neck.","Us ka face changed.","“Where did you get that?”","Aran reached for us ka neza.","Oren raised both hands.","“I knew your walid.”","The old man told them Raan tha alive.","Woh ke paas been captured by Varek.","Aran nearly attacked him se relief aur anger.","Oren continued.","Raan ke paas been taken to the Red Camp, a fortified settlement beyond the western ridge.","Woh tha being forced to explain the Stone Gate.","“Why hasn't Varek killed him?” Aran asked.","“Because your walid hai the only living person who knows how to open it.”","Aran looked at us ka family.","The winter ke paas protected them.","Now winter ke paas become a cage.","Woh needed a mansuba.","Oren said the Red Camp tha guarded by twelve men.","Aran counted un ka hathyars.","Two nezas.","One bow.","A pathar kulhari.","Three knives.","Sera ke paas the best bow.","Benna knew the zameen.","Kian knew the hidden paths.","Woh thay not an army.","Woh did not need to be.","Woh needed to become invisible.","Aran began drawing a map in the dirt.","The rescue would begin ke baad the next toofan."]},{"number":7,"title":"The Red Mark","romanTitle":"Surkh Nishan","meta":"Rust / Clay","en":["The red mark appeared on their door.","It was painted with fresh blood.","Sera wanted to leave immediately.","Aran refused.","“If we run every time they leave a mark, they control where we go.”","Benna nodded.","They waited.","That evening, Oren admitted the truth.","He had once worked for Varek.","He had helped locate villages that possessed old maps.","Aran nearly killed him.","Sera stopped him.","“We need the information.”","Oren explained that Varek believed the old people had hidden a storehouse beneath the Stone Gate. Not food. Not weapons. Something capable of making a tribe independent of the river.","A system of wells, channels and grain chambers.","Water.","Food.","Survival.","Whoever controlled it could survive years of drought.","Aran understood.","The enemy was not chasing a legend.","They were chasing power.","That night a hunter entered their camp.","Aran had expected twelve.","There were twenty.","The attack began with fire arrows.","Their roof caught fire.","Benna pushed Kian toward the escape tunnel.","Sera shot from the doorway.","Aran overturned the storage rack, spilling grain across the floor.","The attackers slipped.","For a moment the family gained an advantage.","Then Varek entered.","He carried a bronze-tipped spear.","“Raan's son.”","Aran stepped forward.","“Where is my father?”","Varek smiled.","“Alive.”","“Bring him.”","“Open the Stone Gate.”","“I don't know how.”","“You carry the key.”","Aran looked at the black stone.","Varek's expression changed.","“Your father gave it to you.”","Aran realized Raan had not given him a keepsake.","He had given him a key.","The fight exploded.","Benna struck one attacker with the stone axe.","Kian pulled a burning hide from the roof and dropped it into a puddle.","Steam filled the room.","Sera and Aran escaped through the rear passage.","Oren stayed behind.","Aran shouted for him.","The old man smiled.","“Run.”","They reached the forest.","Behind them the hut collapsed.","Kian cried.","Benna held him.","Aran looked back at the smoke.","They had lost their shelter.","Most of their food was gone.","Oren was gone.","But now they knew exactly where Raan was.","The Red Camp.","Aran tightened his grip around the black stone.","They would rescue him.","Not because they were strong.","Because they had learned how to survive together."],"ur":["The red mark appeared on un ka darwaza.","It tha painted ke saath fresh khoon.","Sera wanted to leave immediately.","Aran refused.","“If we run every time they leave a mark, they control where we go.”","Benna nodded.","Woh waited.","That evening, Oren admitted the truth.","Woh ke paas once worked for Varek.","Woh ke paas helped locate bastis that possessed old maps.","Aran nearly killed him.","Sera stopped him.","“We need the information.”","Oren explained that Varek believed the old people ke paas hidden a storehouse beneath the Stone Gate. Not khana. Not hathyars. Something capable of making a tribe independent of the darya.","A system of wells, channels aur anaaj chambers.","Pani.","Khana.","Survival.","Whoever controlled it could zinda rehna years of drought.","Aran understood.","The dushman tha not chasing a legend.","Woh thay chasing power.","That raat a shikari entered un ka dera.","Aran ke paas expected twelve.","There thay twenty.","The attack began ke saath aag arrows.","Un ka roof caught aag.","Benna pushed Kian toward the escape tunnel.","Sera shot se the darwazaway.","Aran overturned the storage rack, spilling anaaj across the floor.","The attackers slipped.","For a moment khandan gained an advantage.","Then Varek entered.","Woh carried a bronze-tipped neza.","“Raan's son.”","Aran stepped forward.","“Where hai my walid?”","Varek smiled.","“Alive.”","“Bring him.”","“Open the Stone Gate.”","“I don't know how.”","“You carry the key.”","Aran looked at the black pathar.","Varek's expression changed.","“Your walid gave it to you.”","Aran realized Raan ke paas not given him a keepsake.","Woh ke paas given him a key.","The fight exploded.","Benna struck one attacker ke saath the pathar kulhari.","Kian pulled a burning hide se the roof aur dropped it mein a puddle.","Steam filled the room.","Sera aur Aran escaped through the rear passage.","Oren stayed behind.","Aran shouted for him.","The old man smiled.","“Run.”","Woh reached the jangal.","Behind them the hut collapsed.","Kian cried.","Benna held him.","Aran looked back at the dhuan.","Woh ke paas lost un ka panah.","Most of un ka khana tha gone.","Oren tha gone.","But now they knew exactly where Raan was.","The Red Camp.","Aran tightened us ka grip around the black pathar.","Woh would rescue him.","Not because they thay strong.","Because they ke paas learned how to zinda rehna together."]},{"number":8,"title":"The Storm Wall","romanTitle":"Toofan ki Deewar","meta":"Storm / Slate","en":["The storm arrived three days later.","It came from the west as a wall of black cloud.","Wind tore branches from trees.","Rain turned paths into rivers.","The family reached a high ridge just before the flood entered the valley.","Below them, the old river expanded until it covered fields, trails and abandoned camps.","Then they saw people running.","Ash Hunters.","The same enemy that had hunted them was now trapped by the same storm.","Aran wanted to leave them.","Benna stopped him.","“A storm does not choose sides.”","They watched as several enemy fighters tried to cross the flooded channel.","One child fell.","Kian grabbed Aran's arm.","“We can help.”","Aran hesitated.","The enemy had burned their home.","Varek had taken their father.","But the child was not Varek.","Aran built a rope from twisted hide and vine.","Sera helped him anchor it to a tree.","They pulled the child across.","Then another.","Then an injured man.","When Varek appeared, Aran expected an attack.","Instead the enemy leader simply stared.","“Why?” he asked.","Aran answered, “Because I know what it is to lose family.”","For one moment, Varek looked almost human.","Then the storm forced them apart.","The flood destroyed the Ash Hunters' camp.","It also destroyed the route to the Red Camp.","Aran realized the storm had changed their strategy.","They could no longer attack directly.","They would have to travel through the high country.","During the journey, Kian found a dead tree filled with edible grubs.","Benna roasted them.","Kian refused.","Aran ate one.","Kian ate three.","They laughed until the rain returned.","That night they found shelter in a stone overhang.","Sera told Aran about her brother.","He had been taken by Varek years earlier.","She had spent years believing he was dead.","Aran admitted he was afraid Raan would return changed.","Sera said, “Survival changes everyone.”","“Then what are we trying to save?”","She looked at Benna and Kian sleeping beside the fire.","“This.”","Aran understood.","The goal was not to return to the life they had lost.","The goal was to protect the people they still had.","At dawn they found the Wolf Banner.","Black cloth.","White wolf painted across it.","Varek's strongest fighters used it.","They were close."],"ur":["The toofan arrived three days later.","It came se the west as a wall of black cloud.","Wind tore branches se trees.","Rain turned paths mein daryas.","Khandan reached a high ridge just se pehle the flood entered the wadi.","Below them, the old darya expanded until it covered khets, trails aur abandoned deras.","Then they saw people running.","Ash Hunters.","The same dushman that ke paas hunted them tha now phandaped by the same toofan.","Aran wanted to leave them.","Benna stopped him.","“A toofan does not choose sides.”","Woh watched as several dushman fighters tried to cross the flooded channel.","One child fell.","Kian grabbed Aran's arm.","“We can help.”","Aran hesitated.","The dushman ke paas burned un ka ghar.","Varek ke paas taken un ka walid.","But the child tha not Varek.","Aran built a rope se twisted hide aur vine.","Sera helped him anchor it to a tree.","Woh pulled the child across.","Then another.","Then an injured man.","When Varek appeared, Aran expected an attack.","Instead the dushman leader simply stared.","“Why?” he asked.","Aran answered, “Because I know what it hai to lose family.”","For one moment, Varek looked almost human.","Then the toofan forced them apart.","The flood destroyed the Ash Hunters' dera.","It also destroyed the route to the Red Camp.","Aran realized the toofan ke paas changed un ka strategy.","Woh could no longer attack directly.","Woh would have to travel through the high country.","During the journey, Kian found a dead tree filled ke saath edible grubs.","Benna roasted them.","Kian refused.","Aran ate one.","Kian ate three.","Woh laughed until the barish returned.","That raat they found panah in a pathar overhang.","Sera told Aran about us ka bhai.","Woh ke paas been taken by Varek years earlier.","Woh ke paas spent years believing he tha dead.","Aran admitted he tha afraid Raan would return changed.","Sera said, “Survival changes everyone.”","“Then what hain we trying to save?”","Woh looked at Benna aur Kian sleeping beside the aag.","“This.”","Aran understood.","The goal tha not to return to the zindagi they ke paas lost.","The goal tha to protect the people they still had.","At dawn they found the Wolf Banner.","Black cloth.","White bheriya painted across it.","Varek's strongest fighters used it.","Woh thay close."]},{"number":9,"title":"The Wolf Banner","romanTitle":"Bheriye ka Jhanda","meta":"Night / Iron","en":["The Red Camp stood on a rocky shelf above the valley.","Twelve guards had become twenty after the storm.","Aran watched from the trees.","They had no chance in a direct fight.","So they did not fight.","Sera mapped the guard rotations.","Benna found the water path.","Kian discovered a narrow crawlspace beneath the outer wall.","Aran built a plan.","First, they would cut the camp's water supply.","Second, they would release the goats.","Third, they would create smoke on the western side.","While everyone watched the smoke, Aran and Sera would enter through the crawlspace.","Benna would wait outside with Kian.","If they failed, everyone would run north.","The plan worked.","Mostly.","The goats escaped too early.","The guards shouted.","Smoke filled the camp.","Aran and Sera crawled beneath the wall.","They found Raan in a stone room.","He was thinner.","Older.","But alive.","Aran stopped breathing.","Raan looked up.","For a moment neither moved.","Then Raan smiled.","“You grew.”","Aran hugged him.","All the anger disappeared for one heartbeat.","Then Raan pushed him away.","“You must leave.”","“We're taking you.”","“No. Listen.”","Raan explained that Varek had discovered the Stone Gate but could not open it. The black stone was only half the key.","The other half was beneath the mountain.","The Gate did not protect a treasure.","It protected a water system built by an ancient people after a great drought.","If opened incorrectly, the mountain channels could collapse and flood the entire valley.","Varek did not care.","He wanted control.","Aran understood why the Ash Hunters had destroyed villages.","They were clearing the land around the old system.","Raan had refused to help.","That was why he had been captured.","A horn sounded.","They had been discovered.","Aran freed his father.","Sera found the exit.","Benna and Kian joined them.","The family ran.","Varek appeared at the gate.","He raised his spear.","Raan stepped between him and his sons.","Varek lowered the weapon.","“You always did choose them.”","Raan replied, “That is what makes them stronger than you.”","They escaped into the mountains.","Behind them, the Wolf Banner burned.","But Varek survived."],"ur":["The Red Camp stood on a rocky shelf above the wadi.","Twelve guards ke paas become twenty ke baad the toofan.","Aran watched se the trees.","Woh ke paas no chance in a direct fight.","So they did not fight.","Sera mapped the guard rotations.","Benna found the pani path.","Kian discovered a narrow crawlspace beneath the outer wall.","Aran built a mansuba.","First, they would cut the dera's pani supply.","Second, they would release the goats.","Third, they would create dhuan on the western side.","While everyone watched the dhuan, Aran aur Sera would enter through the crawlspace.","Benna would wait outside ke saath Kian.","If they failed, everyone would run north.","The mansuba worked.","Mostly.","The goats escaped too early.","The guards shouted.","Smoke filled the dera.","Aran aur Sera crawled beneath the wall.","Woh found Raan in a pathar room.","Woh tha thinner.","Older.","But alive.","Aran stopped breathing.","Raan looked up.","For a moment neitus ka moved.","Then Raan smiled.","“You grew.”","Aran hugged him.","All the anger disappeared for one heartbeat.","Then Raan pushed him away.","“You must leave.”","“We're taking you.”","“No. Listen.”","Raan explained that Varek ke paas discovered the Stone Gate lekin could not open it. The black pathar tha only half the key.","The otus ka half tha beneath the pahaar.","The Gate did not protect a treasure.","It protected a pani system built by an ancient people ke baad a great drought.","If opened incorrectly, the pahaar channels could collapse aur flood the entire wadi.","Varek did not care.","Woh wanted control.","Aran understood why the Ash Hunters ke paas destroyed bastis.","Woh thay clearing the zameen around the old system.","Raan ke paas refused to help.","That tha why he ke paas been captured.","A horn sounded.","Woh ke paas been discovered.","Aran freed us ka walid.","Sera found the exit.","Benna aur Kian joined them.","Khandan ran.","Varek appeared at the gate.","Woh raised us ka neza.","Raan stepped between him aur us ka sons.","Varek lowered the hathyar.","“You always did choose them.”","Raan replied, “That hai what makes them stronger than you.”","Woh escaped mein the pahaars.","Behind them, the Wolf Banner burned.","But Varek zinda rehnad."]},{"number":10,"title":"The Last Hunt","romanTitle":"Aakhri Shikar","meta":"Ember / Ash","en":["The Stone Gate was hidden behind a waterfall.","Raan led them through a narrow passage.","Inside were channels cut into stone, reservoirs and clay pipes.","The ancient builders had created a system that collected mountain water and carried it into three valleys.","There were also underground chambers filled with sealed grain jars.","Not gold.","Not weapons.","A way for ordinary families to survive.","Benna touched the walls.","“People fought over this?”","Raan nodded.","“People fight over whatever keeps children alive.”","Aran found the central mechanism.","It required two stones.","His black stone and the copper bracelet from the Valley of Bones.","He placed both into carved sockets.","The Gate opened.","Water thundered through the channels.","The mountain shook.","Raan shouted for everyone to run.","A wall cracked.","Sera pulled Kian away.","Benna grabbed the grain jars.","Aran refused to leave without the map.","Raan dragged him outside.","The chamber collapsed.","The old system survived.","But the Stone Gate was sealed again beneath tons of rock.","They had lost the ancient map.","They had lost most of the supplies.","Yet they had something more important.","A functioning water channel had opened in the valley.","Fresh water began flowing toward the abandoned fields.","Families could survive there.","Raan looked at his sons.","“This is why the old people built it.”","Aran looked toward the horizon.","Smoke rose from the south.","Varek was coming.","The final battle would not be about a gate.","It would be about who controlled the valley."],"ur":["The Stone Gate tha hidden ke peeche a panifall.","Raan led them through a narrow passage.","Inside thay channels cut mein pathar, reservoirs aur clay pipes.","The ancient builders ke paas created a system that collected pahaar pani aur carried it mein three wadis.","There thay also underground chambers filled ke saath sealed anaaj jars.","Not gold.","Not hathyars.","A way for ordinary families to zinda rehna.","Benna touched the walls.","“People fought over this?”","Raan nodded.","“People fight over whatever keeps bachay alive.”","Aran found the central mechanism.","It required two pathars.","Us ka black pathar aur the copper bracelet se the Wadi of Bones.","Woh placed both mein carved sockets.","The Gate opened.","Pani thundered through the channels.","The pahaar shook.","Raan shouted for everyone to run.","A wall cracked.","Sera pulled Kian away.","Benna grabbed the anaaj jars.","Aran refused to leave ke baghair the map.","Raan dragged him outside.","The chamber collapsed.","The old system zinda rehnad.","But the Stone Gate tha sealed again beneath tons of rock.","Woh ke paas lost the ancient map.","Woh ke paas lost most of the supplies.","Yet they ke paas something more important.","A functioning pani channel ke paas opened in the wadi.","Fresh pani began flowing toward the abandoned khets.","Families could zinda rehna there.","Raan looked at us ka sons.","“Tus ka hai why the old people built it.”","Aran looked toward the horizon.","Smoke rose se the south.","Varek tha coming.","The final battle would not be about a gate.","It would be about who controlled the wadi."]},{"number":11,"title":"The Stone Gate","romanTitle":"Pathar ka Darwaza","meta":"Gold / Ochre","en":["The final hunt began before sunrise.","Aran knew Varek's fighters were exhausted.","The valley was flooded in places, dry in others.","Aran used the terrain as a weapon.","They placed sharpened stakes near the narrow pass.","They dug pits beneath loose grass.","They stored stones above the slope.","Benna organized the families who had joined them.","Sera trained the hunters to move in pairs.","Raan taught them one rule.","“Never chase a man who is running away.”","The enemy arrived at noon.","Varek led them.","He had fewer men than before.","But he was desperate.","The first attack hit the false path.","Two men fell into pits.","The second group was forced toward the river.","Aran released the stored water.","The ground became mud.","The enemy lost formation.","Sera's archers fired.","Nobody chased.","Varek reached the ridge.","He and Aran faced each other.","Varek's bronze spear was better.","Aran's stone spear was lighter.","They fought among the rocks.","Varek struck Aran's shoulder.","Aran fell.","Varek raised his spear.","Kian threw the stone axe.","Varek turned.","Aran moved.","He drove the spear into the ground beside Varek's foot, trapping the man's cloak beneath the shaft.","Varek fell.","Aran could have killed him.","Instead he stepped back.","“Leave.”","Varek stared.","“Mercy makes you weak.”","Aran answered, “No. It gives me a choice.”","Varek escaped into the northern forest.","The valley belonged to the families.","For the first time, there was enough water.","There was enough grain.","There were fields that could be planted.","Raan watched Aran distribute food before taking his own portion.","He smiled.","“Now you understand.”","That evening the family sat together.","Benna cooked meat.","Kian complained about the taste.","Sera laughed.","Raan looked toward the mountains.","“The Stone Gate was only the beginning.”","Aran looked at him.","“Beginning of what?”","Raan pointed beyond the mountains.","“There are other valleys.”","The season was not finished."],"ur":["The final hunt began se pehle surajrise.","Aran knew Varek's fighters thay exhausted.","The wadi tha flooded in places, dry in others.","Aran used the terbarish as a hathyar.","Woh placed sharpened stakes near the narrow pass.","Woh dug pits beneath loose grass.","Woh stored pathars above the slope.","Benna organized the families who ke paas joined them.","Sera tbarished the shikaris to move in pairs.","Raan taught them one rule.","“Never chase a man who hai running away.”","The dushman arrived at noon.","Varek led them.","Woh ke paas fewer men than before.","But he tha desperate.","The first attack hit the false path.","Two men fell mein pits.","The second group tha forced toward the darya.","Aran released the stored pani.","The ground became mud.","The dushman lost formation.","Sera's archers aagd.","Nobody chased.","Varek reached the ridge.","Woh aur Aran faced each other.","Varek's bronze neza tha better.","Aran's pathar neza tha lighter.","Woh fought among the rocks.","Varek struck Aran's shoulder.","Aran fell.","Varek raised us ka neza.","Kian threw the pathar kulhari.","Varek turned.","Aran moved.","Woh drove the neza mein the ground beside Varek's foot, phandaping the man's cloak beneath the shaft.","Varek fell.","Aran could have killed him.","Instead he stepped back.","“Leave.”","Varek stared.","“Mercy makes you weak.”","Aran answered, “No. It gives me a choice.”","Varek escaped mein the northern jangal.","The wadi belonged to the families.","For the first time, there tha enough pani.","There tha enough anaaj.","There thay khets that could be mansubated.","Raan watched Aran distribute khana se pehle taking us ka own portion.","Woh smiled.","“Now you understand.”","That evening khandan sat together.","Benna cooked gosht.","Kian complained about the taste.","Sera laughed.","Raan looked toward the pahaars.","“The Stone Gate tha only the beginning.”","Aran looked at him.","“Beginning of what?”","Raan pointed beyond the pahaars.","“There hain otus ka wadis.”","The season tha not finished."]},{"number":12,"title":"The First Dawn","romanTitle":"Pehli Subah","meta":"Dawn / Sand","en":["The first dawn after the battle felt strangely quiet. No horns. No shouting. No smoke. Children returned to the river, hunters repaired tools, and families cleared the old fields. For the first time, the valley did not feel like a hiding place. It felt like home.","Aran carved their story into a flat piece of wood. He wrote about the fire, the river, the hunger, the storm, the rescue of Raan and the battle at the pass. He did not write that he had been brave. He wrote the names of the people who had stood beside him.","Raan watched him work. “Why record it?” he asked.","“Because people forget.”","Raan nodded. “Then remember the truth, not only the victories.”","He finally told his family everything. The ancient builders had survived a terrible drought by connecting mountain reservoirs, underground grain chambers and irrigation channels. Their knowledge had made villages rich enough to survive years without rain. Then people began fighting over the system. Water became power. Power became war. The surviving guardians buried the Stone Gate and divided its maps so no single ruler could control the valleys again.","The black stone was one half of that old key. The copper bracelet was another. The final piece was still missing.","Aran stared at him. “Where?”","Raan pointed north.","“Beyond the Wolf Mountains.”","For once, Aran did not immediately answer.","He thought about the family sleeping below. Benna had spent years keeping them fed. Kian was finally laughing again. Sera had become part of the household without anyone formally asking her to stay. The valley had water. It had fields. It had safety.","They had something worth losing.","Weeks passed. The first barley shoots appeared. Kian celebrated as if he had planted every seed himself. Benna organized food stores. Raan repaired the channels. Sera trained young hunters. Aran taught them to build traps, read tracks and move without wasting energy.","The family had become a community.","Then a messenger arrived from the western ridge.","He carried a piece of black cloth.","The Wolf Banner.","Varek had survived.","Worse, he had joined another clan beyond the mountains. They were gathering men, animals and weapons. The messenger had seen bronze blades among them, better than anything in the valley.","Aran looked at Raan.","“How many?”","“Enough.”","That night the family ate together. There was roasted deer, barley, roots and a small bowl of berries Kian had gathered himself.","Nobody spoke about war.","For one evening, they chose peace.","After the meal, Kian sat beside Aran.","“Do you remember the first night?”","Aran smiled.","“I remember all of them.”","Kian looked at the stars.","“Do you think Father will always be here now?”","Aran looked at Raan across the fire.","“I hope so.”","The answer was honest.","Before sunrise, Aran walked to the ridge.","Three columns of smoke rose beyond the northern horizon.","Three signals.","Three groups moving toward Auran.","Raan joined him.","“They found us.”","Aran gripped his spear.","Below them, the valley was waking. Fires appeared one by one. Families carried water. Hunters checked their bows. Children ran between shelters.","This was no longer the frightened family that had crossed the river with three water skins.","They had built something.","And now they would have to defend it.","Aran looked toward the mountains.","The first season had taught him how to survive.","The next would teach him how to lead.","Behind the ridge, hidden beneath ancient stone, the remaining half of the old map waited.","And somewhere beyond the Wolf Mountains, someone else was already searching for it.","The Auran Chronicles had survived their first season.","The war for Auran had just begun."],"ur":["The first dawn ke baad the battle felt strangely quiet. No horns. No shouting. No dhuan. Children returned to the darya, shikaris repaired auzars, aur families cleared the old khets. For the first time, the wadi did not feel like a hiding place. It felt like ghar.","Aran carved un ka story mein a flat piece of wood. Woh wrote about the aag, the darya, the hunger, the toofan, the rescue of Raan aur the battle at the pass. Woh did not write that he ke paas been brave. Woh wrote the names of the people who ke paas stood beside him.","Raan watched him work. “Why record it?” he asked.","“Because people forget.”","Raan nodded. “Then remember the truth, not only the victories.”","Woh finally told us ka family everything. The ancient builders ke paas zinda rehnad a terrible drought by connecting pahaar reservoirs, underground anaaj chambers aur irrigation channels. Un ka knowledge ke paas made bastis rich enough to zinda rehna years ke baghair barish. Then people began fighting over the system. Pani became power. Power became war. The surviving guardians buried the Stone Gate aur divided its maps so no single ruler could control the wadis again.","The black pathar tha one half of that old key. The copper bracelet tha another. The final piece tha still missing.","Aran stared at him. “Where?”","Raan pointed north.","“Beyond the Wolf Pahaar.”","For once, Aran did not immediately answer.","Woh thought about khandan sleeping below. Benna ke paas spent years keeping them fed. Kian tha finally laughing again. Sera ke paas become part of the household ke baghair anyone formally asking us ka to stay. The wadi ke paas pani. It ke paas khets. It ke paas safety.","Woh ke paas something worth losing.","Weeks passed. The first barley shoots appeared. Kian celebrated as if he ke paas mansubated every seed himself. Benna organized khana stores. Raan repaired the channels. Sera tbarished young shikaris. Aran taught them to build phandas, read tracks aur move ke baghair wasting energy.","Khandan ke paas become a community.","Then a messenger arrived se the western ridge.","Woh carried a piece of black cloth.","The Wolf Banner.","Varek ke paas zinda rehnad.","Worse, he ke paas joined anotus ka qabeela beyond the pahaars. Woh thay gathering men, animals aur hathyars. The messenger ke paas seen bronze blades among them, better than anything in the wadi.","Aran looked at Raan.","“How many?”","“Enough.”","That raat khandan ate together. There tha roasted deer, barley, roots aur a small bowl of berries Kian ke paas gathered himself.","Nobody spoke about war.","For one evening, they chose peace.","After the khana, Kian sat beside Aran.","“Do you remember the first raat?”","Aran smiled.","“I remember all of them.”","Kian looked at the stars.","“Do you think Fatus ka will always be here now?”","Aran looked at Raan across the aag.","“I hope so.”","The answer tha honest.","Before surajrise, Aran walked to the ridge.","Three columns of dhuan rose beyond the northern horizon.","Three signals.","Three groups moving toward Auran.","Raan joined him.","“Woh found us.”","Aran gripped us ka neza.","Below them, the wadi tha waking. Aags appeared one by one. Families carried pani. Hunters checked un ka bows. Children ran between panahs.","Tus ka tha no longer the frightened family that ke paas crossed the darya ke saath three pani skins.","Woh ke paas built something.","And now they would have to defend it.","Aran looked toward the pahaars.","The first season ke paas taught him how to zinda rehna.","The next would teach him how to lead.","Behind the ridge, hidden beneath ancient pathar, the remaining half of the old map waited.","And somewhere beyond the Wolf Pahaar, someone else tha already searching for it.","The Auran Chronicles ke paas zinda rehnad un ka first season.","The war for Auran ke paas just begun."]}];


const UI={
 en:{eyebrow:"A SURVIVAL CHRONICLE",heroSub:"A family. A forgotten valley. A world that wants them dead.",continue:"CONTINUE THE CHRONICLE",scroll:"Scroll to enter Auran",introEyebrow:"THE YEAR IS 3000 BC",introTitle:"Before kingdoms had borders, survival had a price.",introText:"Auran is a land of rivers, high grass, stone ridges and hungry winters. Families hunt together, trade by firelight and sleep with weapons within reach. Beyond their valleys move rival clans, predators and men who have learned that fear is a useful weapon.",chaptersEyebrow:"THE FIRST SEASON",chaptersTitle:"Twelve nights. One family.",chaptersText:"Read in order. Every episode changes the road ahead.",chapters:"CHAPTERS",previous:"PREVIOUS",next:"NEXT",read:"READ EPISODE",completed:"COMPLETED",notCompleted:"NOT COMPLETED"},
 ur:{eyebrow:"AIK SURVIVAL KI DASTAAN",heroSub:"Ek khandan. Ek bhooli hui wadi. Aur ek duniya jo unhein zinda nahi dekhna chahti.",continue:"DASTAAN JARI RAKHEIN",scroll:"Auran mein dakhil hon",introEyebrow:"SAAL 3000 QABL-E-MASEEH",introTitle:"Badshahaton ki sarhaden banne se pehle, zinda rehne ki qeemat thi.",introText:"Auran daryon, unchi ghaas, pathari ridges aur sakht sardiyon ki zameen hai. Khandan mil kar shikar karte, aag ke paas tijarat karte aur hathyar paas rakh kar sote hain. Wadiyon se bahar dushman qabeelay, darinday aur woh log ghoomte hain jo khauf ko hathyar banana seekh chuke hain.",chaptersEyebrow:"PEHLA SEASON",chaptersTitle:"Barah raatain. Ek khandan.",chaptersText:"Tarteeb se parhein. Har episode agla raasta badal deta hai.",chapters:"EPISODES",previous:"PEECHLA",next:"AGLA",read:"EPISODE PARHEIN",completed:"MUKAMMAL",notCompleted:"ABHI BAQI"}}
let lang=localStorage.getItem("auranLang")||"en";
let current=Number(localStorage.getItem("auranCurrent")||0);
const done=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem("auranDone")||"[]");
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
function applyUI(){
 document.querySelectorAll("[data-i18n]").forEach(el=>{const k=el.dataset.i18n;if(UI[lang][k])el.textContent=UI[lang][k]});
 $("#languageToggle").textContent=lang==="en"?"ROMAN URDU":"ENGLISH";
 document.documentElement.lang=lang==="en"?"en":"ur";
 renderCards();
 if(!$("#reader").classList.contains("hidden"))renderReader(false);
}
function renderCards(){
 const grid=$("#chapterGrid"); grid.innerHTML="";
 STORY.forEach((ep,i)=>{
  const card=document.createElement("button"); card.className="card"; card.style.setProperty("--card",`hsl(${28+i*4}deg 18% ${24+i%3*3}%)`);
  card.innerHTML=`<div><div class="card-num">${String(ep.number).padStart(2,"0")} · ${lang==="en"?"EPISODE":"EPISODE"}</div><h3>${lang==="en"?ep.title:ep.romanTitle}</h3><p>${ep.meta}</p></div><div class="card-bottom"><span class="card-read">${done.includes(i)?UI[lang].completed:UI[lang].read}</span><span>↗</span></div>`;
  card.addEventListener("click",()=>openEpisode(i));
  grid.appendChild(card);
 });
}
function openEpisode(i){
 current=i;localStorage.setItem("auranCurrent",i);
 $("#chapters").classList.add("hidden");$("#reader").classList.remove("hidden");
 renderReader(true);window.scrollTo({top:$("#reader").offsetTop-20,behavior:"smooth"});
}
function renderReader(scroll){
 const ep=STORY[current], paras=ep[lang==="en"?"en":"ur"];
 $("#readerNumber").textContent=`EPISODE ${String(ep.number).padStart(2,"0")}`;
 $("#readerTitle").textContent=lang==="en"?ep.title:ep.romanTitle;
 $("#readerMeta").textContent=ep.meta;
 $("#story").innerHTML=paras.map((p,i)=>`<p>${escapeHTML(p)}</p>${(i+1)%7===0?'<div class="scene-break">· · ·</div>':''}`).join("");
 $("#prevBtn").disabled=current===0;$("#nextBtn").disabled=current===STORY.length-1;
 $("#completion").textContent=done.includes(current)?`✓ ${UI[lang].completed}`:`${UI[lang].notCompleted}`;
 document.body.className=`episode-theme-${current+1}`;
 $("#episodeProgress").style.width="0%";
 if(scroll) window.scrollTo({top:$("#reader").offsetTop-20,behavior:"smooth"});
}
function escapeHTML(s){return s.replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({"&":"&amp;","<":"&lt;",">":"&gt;",'"':"&quot;","'":"&#039;"}[c]))}
function markDone(){
 if(!done.includes(current)){done.push(current);localStorage.setItem("auranDone",JSON.stringify(done))}
 $("#completion").textContent=`✓ ${UI[lang].completed}`;renderCards();
}
function updateProgress(){
 const r=$("#reader"); if(r.classList.contains("hidden"))return;
 const top=r.offsetTop, height=r.scrollHeight-window.innerHeight;
 const pct=Math.max(0,Math.min(100,((window.scrollY-top)/height)*100));
 $("#episodeProgress").style.width=pct+"%";
 $("#progress").style.width=pct+"%";
 if(pct>88)markDone();
}
$("#languageToggle").addEventListener("click",()=>{lang=lang==="en"?"ur":"en";localStorage.setItem("auranLang",lang);applyUI()});
$("#continueBtn").addEventListener("click",()=>openEpisode(current));
$("#backBtn").addEventListener("click",()=>{$("#reader").classList.add("hidden");$("#chapters").classList.remove("hidden");window.scrollTo({top:$("#chapters").offsetTop-20,behavior:"smooth"})});
$("#prevBtn").addEventListener("click",()=>{if(current>0)openEpisode(current-1)});
$("#nextBtn").addEventListener("click",()=>{if(current<STORY.length-1)openEpisode(current+1)});
window.addEventListener("scroll",updateProgress,{passive:true});
applyUI();
